<title>ITALY: Italian bonds/futures closing report.</title>
<headline>Italian bonds/futures closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian bonds and futures surged on Friday with the December Liffe Btp contract touching 124.18 and three and five-year Btp cash bonds at new highs, before falling back as late profit-taking set in, traders said.</p>
<p>Next resistance for the Btp future was seen at 124.37, a record high set on October 9.</p>
<p>Traders said prices soared not only in line with other markets but also due to short-covering by operators who &quot;faced with the strong rise in bunds decided to abandon their uncovered positions.&quot;</p>
</text>
